---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/astro/Breadcrumb.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Gibraltar For Sale — About" description="About the Gibraltar For Sale first release: locally specific area guides, practical buyer resources and a commitment to verify listings and data before publication.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px] px-5 pb-20 pt-10 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-16">
    <p class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-sea-700">About this guide</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink-900 sm:text-6xl">A clearer view of property in Gibraltar</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-stone-600">Gibraltar For Sale is being developed as an independent property guide for people comparing areas, learning how a purchase works and planning a move. The first public release focuses on practical local context and sourced buyer information.</p>
    <div class="article-content mt-10">
      <h2 id="what-is-here">What is in the first release</h2>
      <p>There are eight area guides and a collection of practical articles about buying, costs, residence, mortgages, renting, viewings and new builds. The market pages explain which evidence is needed before an estimate is useful. Citations and source links are kept with the relevant guidance so readers can check details directly.</p>
      <h2 id="what-is-not-here">What is not live yet</h2>
      <p>No verified property listings, agent directory, developer information, public enquiry form, email alert system or current private-market dataset has been supplied. We do not display fictional property or partner details as real. The listings and market pages say when the underlying evidence is unavailable.</p>
      <h2 id="how-we-approach-claims">How we approach claims</h2>
      <p>Property status and price should be tied to a source and update date. Legal, tax and residence matters should point to official information and qualified local advice. General website guidance cannot decide eligibility, value a particular home or replace a solicitor, accountant, lender or immigration professional.</p>
      <h2 id="future-development">What comes next</h2>
      <p>Listings and contact services can be added only after genuine inventory, responsible agent attribution, operator details, privacy arrangements and working lead delivery are in place. Until then, this is an information-first site with no public form collecting a buyer’s personal details.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
